title: Gheist Campaign Automated ci-sync Branch Creation via Stolen GitHub Tokens
id: 27f61d2d-e4b4-491d-8cf2-faff45cdc59a
status: experimental
description: Detects developer-endpoint git activity consistent with the Gheist automated campaign, which abuses stolen GitHub tokens to plant ci-sync-<6 alphanumeric> branches and sync-check.yml workflows in order to extract private repository secrets from Actions logs (Wiz Research, 13,500+ branches across 850+ tokens since September 15, 2026).
references:
  - https://www.wiz.io/blog/gheist-attempted-scaled-abuse-of-stolen-github-tokens-stumbles
  - https://linuxmint.hu/hir/2026/10/gheist-ellopott-github-tokenekkel-szerez-privat-repok-titkait-az-actions-naploibol
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/10/27
tags:
  - attack.t1078
  - attack.t1552
  - attack.t1195
  - attack.t1132
logsource:
  category: process_creation
  product: windows
detection:
  selection_git_branch:
    Image|endswith:
      - '\git.exe'
      - '\git-remote-https.exe'
    CommandLine|contains:
      - 'ci-sync-'
      - 'sync-check.yml'
  condition: selection_git_branch
falsepositives:
  - Internal CI synchronisation tooling that legitimately names branches ci-sync-*
  - Developer scripts that push the same workflow filename
level: medium
